.TH XUR.STD.HTTP 7 "2026-10-29" "xur 0.1.2" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.http \- HTTP client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B use std::http;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::http
provides a synchronous HTTP client backed by ureq.
Requests return
.BR "Result<Response, str>" .
.SH SHORTHAND FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B http::get(url) -> Result<Response, str>
Send a GET request.
.TP
.B http::post(url) -> Result<Response, str>
.TQ
.B http::post(url, body) -> Result<Response, str>
Send a POST request, optionally with a string or bytes body.
.TP
.B http::put(url) / http::put(url, body)
Send a PUT request.
.TP
.B http::patch(url) / http::patch(url, body)
Send a PATCH request.
.TP
.B http::delete(url) -> Result<Response, str>
Send a DELETE request.
.TP
.B http::head(url) -> Result<Response, str>
Send a HEAD request.
.SH REQUEST BUILDER
.TP
.B http::request(method, url) -> RequestBuilder
Create a builder for an arbitrary HTTP method.
.SS RequestBuilder methods
All builder methods return a new RequestBuilder (immutable builder pattern).
.TP
.B header(name, value) -> RequestBuilder
Add a header.
.TP
.B bearer_auth(token) -> RequestBuilder
Set the Authorization header to
.BI "Bearer " token .
.TP
.B basic_auth(username, password) -> RequestBuilder
Set the Authorization header to
.BI "Basic " base64(username:password) .
.TP
.B body(data) -> RequestBuilder
Set the request body (string or bytes).
.TP
.B json_body(value) -> RequestBuilder
Serialize
.I value
as JSON, set the body and Content-Type.
.TP
.B query(key, value) -> RequestBuilder
Append a URL query parameter.
.TP
.B timeout(seconds) -> RequestBuilder
Set the request timeout in seconds (default 30).
.TP
.B send() -> Result<Response, str>
Execute the request.
.SH RESPONSE
.TP
.B status() -> int
The HTTP status code.
.TP
.B status_text() -> str
The reason phrase (e.g.\& "OK", "Not Found").
.TP
.B url() -> str
The final URL after any redirects.
.TP
.B text() -> str
The response body as a UTF-8 string.
.TP
.B bytes() -> bytes
The response body as raw bytes.
.TP
.B json() -> Result<value, str>
Parse the response body as JSON.
.TP
.B header(name) -> Option<str>
Look up a response header by name (case-insensitive).
.TP
.B headers() -> record
All response headers as a record.
.SH EXAMPLES
Simple GET:
.PP
.nf
use std::http;
use std::io;

fn main() -> Result<()> {
    let resp = http::get("https://httpbin.org/get")?;
    io::println("status: {}", resp.status());
    io::println("body: {}", resp.text());
    Ok(())
}
.fi
.PP
POST JSON with authentication:
.PP
.nf
use std::http;
use std::io;

fn main() -> Result<()> {
    let data = @{ name: "xur" };
    let resp = http::request("POST", "https://httpbin.org/post")
        .bearer_auth("token")
        .json_body(data)
        .send()?;
    io::println("{}", resp.json()?.data);
    Ok(())
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7),
.BR xur.std.json (7),
.BR xur.std.net (7)
